    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vomiting and diarrhea since yesterday, with tightenings of the bump, at 22 weeks with twins. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Cleopatra is a 29-year-old woman, gravida 2 para 1, at 22 weeks 0 days with a dichorionic diamniotic twin pregnancy, who came in the same day after a day and a half of vomiting (five times yesterday, once this morning) and watery diarrhea about six times a day, after a meal at which two of her guests became ill in the same way. Since last night she has felt painless tightenings of the bump about twice an hour, which ease when she rests and drinks. She has had no bleeding, no leaking of fluid, no pelvic pressure, no period-like or back pain, and no fever above 37.5 C. Both babies are moving. She has kept down small sips of an oral rehydration drink since the early morning but is passing less urine. She takes aspirin 81 mg at bedtime, ferrous sulfate every other day, and a prenatal vitamin; she stopped the doxylamine with pyridoxine three weeks ago. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>A day and a half ago</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Vomiting, watery diarrhea, painless tightenings about twice an hour</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Two guests from the same meal have the same illness</td></tr><tr><td>Pertinent negatives</td><td>No bleeding, leaking fluid, pelvic pressure, period-like or back pain, blood in the stool, or high fever</td></tr><tr><td>Fetal movement</td><td>Both babies moving</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
