    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 2026-06-02; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Tired but alert; temperature 37.4 C; heart rate 98 seated and 104 standing; blood pressure 102/60 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Mouth</td><td>Mucous membranes slightly dry</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft; mild diffuse tenderness above the uterus; uterus soft and non-tender between tightenings, fundal height 25 cm, consistent with twins at 22 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Fetal</td><td>Fetal hearts 148 and 142 per minute by Doppler</td></tr><tr><td>Monitoring</td><td>Tocodynamometry for 40 minutes: two mild painless tightenings, settling with oral fluids</td></tr><tr><td>Cervix</td><td>Transvaginal cervical length 39 mm (41 mm at 19 weeks); closed os; no funneling</td></tr><tr><td>Urinalysis</td><td>Ketones 1+, specific gravity 1.025; nitrite and leukocyte esterase negative; protein negative</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

