    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral gastroenteritis with mild dehydration (O98.512)</content>. Probably norovirus, given the shared meal. Mild dehydration with ketonuria; sodium 135 mmol/L, potassium 3.5 mmol/L, and creatinine 0.55 mg/dL. Dehydration can bring on uterine irritability; the tightenings are infrequent and settling, the cervix is long and closed and unchanged, and there is no bleeding or leaking, so this is not preterm labor. No stool tests or antibiotics are needed. [S]<list><item>Oral rehydration solution in small, frequent sips, at least 2 to 3 liters a day while the diarrhea lasts, then a normal diet.</item><item>No anti-diarrheal medicine; ondansetron is not needed because the vomiting is settling.</item><item>Hand washing and bleach-based cleaning; no preparing food for others until two days after the symptoms stop.</item><item>Come in at once for regular or painful tightenings (four or more an hour), bleeding, leaking fluid, pelvic pressure, inability to keep fluids down, fainting, or reduced movements.</item><item>Nurse telephone check tomorrow.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Twin pregnancy, dichorionic diamniotic (O30.041)</content>. Fetal hearts 148 and 142 per minute; fundal height consistent with twins at 22 weeks; cervical length stable. [S]<list><item>Hold aspirin and iron tonight if she is still vomiting, and restart tomorrow.</item><item>Prenatal visit with the growth scan and glucose challenge at 25 weeks as planned.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Multifetal Gestations: Twin, Triplet, and Higher-Order Multifetal Pregnancies: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 231 (2021); Prediction and Prevention of Spontaneous Preterm Birth: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 234 (2021); 2017 Infectious Diseases Society of America Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Management of Infectious Diarrhea (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse telephone check tomorrow; prenatal visit at 25 weeks as planned; at once for the warning signs above. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-23: prenatal visit at 25 weeks: growth scan, glucose challenge, and blood count. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
